>>At that stage (i.e. with Amulet) the only difference would be that in the
>>scroll case you have to reach the stairs first which probably could require
>>some scrolls; if that was your point.
> 
> Yes. If one want to really avoid the level (because it's filled with the
> summoning storm of a Titan), potion will be a better way than
> scrolls/wand/spell since it's guaranteed to work and you have no risk to
> accidentally land in a room filled with nasties.

Well, you have the risk a level above. But true, if you assume the titan
already summoned. It's helpful to have the potion as an option then.

Though there are some downsides; potions are IIRC four times as heavy as
scrolls and three times as heavy as wands. Then, as Jakob mentioned, they
are much less frequent than the scrolls (or wands). The rare potions are
also generally better used for alchemy, IMO, to create lots of full healing
potions, which are quite necessary for the endgame.

I agree, it is a good application to use the potion for emergency escapes.
Though up to the middle game cursed scrolls of teleport will be available
more often to achieve that. After you have the Amulet and still in Gehennom
they are unreliable; nevertheless there is the notable exception of non-
teleport levels. So, I'd say, they are of some but limited applicability
here.

Another interesting and fun application is to leave the potion for some
tough monster at the floor, at best on the first level in Vlads tower or
Sokoban. ;-)

